From 031aa398883c06c9761261f5bcfe4df0411d873b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: testbed <hello@paul.church>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 12:40:28 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] fix(network): gate the testbed behind a feature and fix
 its security and correctness issues

- Put link emulation, the upload scheduler and the testbed constants behind an
  off-by-default `testbed` feature; normal builds use plain TcpStream and the
  original timeouts, inbound interval and localhost check.
- Keep zebra-relay out of the workspace so the feature never unifies into zebrad.
- Close a connection's socket when its stream is dropped, bound user-space
  buffering to the emulated link, and forward socket read errors.
- Scheduler: serve waits over 500 ms first, cap gate waits at 2 s, serve repeated
  requests last, measure only replies to our own block requests, release slots via
  RAII, reject non-finite estimates, and bound and expire the estimate map.
- Relay: limit in-flight downloads (200, one per advertiser IP), keep a bounded
  block store, cap the event log, and refuse non-loopback addresses.
- Add regression tests for each fix.
